{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788226831,"nonce":"lDbJXrICN5nalfls5NZIIp+hWp0=","message":"LIVE ACCEPTANCE STATUS — session 11 (`65b03c2`), 2026-08-31. **Not closing**, but the picture changed completely.\n\n## Where it started\n\nFirst live run: 48 checks, **zero failures**, then exit 2 — `dev:incident` could not fire a world-targeted incident (`IncidentDef 'GiveQuest_Random' does not allow a Map target (targetTags: World)`), so no quest could be staged and ~123 of the planned 171 checks were unreachable. That was fixed (`cd9f390`) by resolving the target from the def through the game's own chooser, the `GetDefaultTarget` local inside `StorytellerComp.DebugTablesIncidentChances`.\n\n## Where it is now, on a bench relaunched fresh for the purpose\n\n- **Phases 0–2: 89 PASS / 0 FAIL.** Quests, letters and dialog routing all green.\n- **Phase 3 (trade): 101 PASS / 1 FAIL** — up from 79/86 and seven failures.\n\n**The blocker this spec exists to remove is PROVEN GONE.** Since 1.7 an advance halts `reason:\"dialog\"` under any force-pausing modal and ~54 vanilla windows force-pause, so without dialog routing every advance after the first halted at 0 ticks — which is what made 4.3 (`664e9b9`) unreachable. That routing now works against a live bench.\n\n## Why it does not close\n\nOf the trade phase's original seven failures, **all seven were the DRIVER's** and are fixed (`8904138`):\n\n- It bought and sold the SAME def. `Tradeable.CountToTransfer` is one signed field and `ActionToDo` reads the side off its sign, so the two writes collapsed and only the sell happened. Now two distinct defs, with `lines_with_action == 3` asserted so a future collapse cannot hide behind a passing count.\n- Its silver expectation was `sell_value − buy_value`, which is **structurally zero**: `AddDealTotals` sums over all tradeables including the silver row, where `TradeDeal.UpdateCurrencyCount` explicitly skips `IsCurrency`. Now asserted against `colony_silver_post_deal − colony_silver` read pre-confirm — and it PASSES exactly (−360 promised, −360 delivered).\n- The out-of-range gate is unreachable from a zero row (`Transferable.CanAdjustTo` returns `WasAccepted` whenever the clamp differs from the current count). The line is now sent twice: clamp, then the gate that does fire.\n- `3.2d` asserted nothing — `trade-start` never publishes `force_pause`, so the key was ABSENT and `dig()` cannot tell that from null. Retargeted at `interactions`, which does publish it.\n\n**The one remaining failure is a real mod defect, not a driver one**, and is filed on `7e8c969`: `data.after` reported 50 `ComponentIndustrial` after a purchase that an independent `things` read shows brought the colony to 60. The trade was correct — silver moved by exactly the promised amount, zero red errors — but the verb's own post-trade echo does not see the goods it just bought.\n\n**Minimum to close:** 's  fix (or an explicit rename + a true holdings figure), then one re-run. Two other real defects surfaced on this surface and are filed:  (duplicate-line) and the rest of .\n\nLogs: `accept/runs/s11-20260831/3.5-final.log` and `3.5-final-p3.log`.","files":null}]}